---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const hasAnalytics = Boolean(SITE.analyticsSnippet);
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How AIERA-TS handles your information: what we collect, why, and the choices you have.">
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap page-inner">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated November 7, 2026.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Your privacy matters. AIERA-TS is a reading-first blog, so we collect as little as possible. This page explains what that is, why we need it and the choices you have.</p>

        <h2>Reading the blog</h2>
        <p>You can read every article without an account, and we don't use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
        <p>The site remembers two small preferences in your own browser: your light or dark theme and your colour palette. These stay on your device, are never sent to us, and you can clear them at any time through your browser settings.</p>
        {hasAnalytics
          ? <p>We use privacy-friendly analytics to count page views and see which articles are most helpful. It doesn't use cookies, doesn't follow you across other websites and doesn't identify you personally.</p>
          : <p>We don't currently use analytics. If we add it in future, we'll choose a privacy-friendly service that doesn't use cookies or follow you across other websites, and we'll update this page first.</p>}

        <h2>The newsletter</h2>
        <p>If you subscribe, we store your email address so we can send you each weekly issue. We don't ask for any other personal information.</p>
        <p>Your address is used only for the AIERA-TS newsletter. We never sell, rent or share it. Every issue includes an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing removes you from our mailing list.</p>

        <h2>Services we rely on</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Buttondown</strong> delivers the newsletter and stores subscriber addresses on our behalf. See the <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy">Buttondown privacy policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts the site. Like most web hosts, it briefly processes technical information such as your IP address to deliver pages securely. See the <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify privacy policy</a>.</li>
          {hasAnalytics && <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> counts page views without cookies or personal profiles, so we can see which articles are most helpful. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</li>}
          <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> provides the site's typefaces, so your browser connects to Google's servers to load them. See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Articles link to other websites for sources and further reading. Those sites have their own privacy policies.</p>

        <h2>Keeping information safe</h2>
        <p>The site is served over a secure connection (HTTPS), and we keep the information we hold to a minimum.</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>AIERA-TS is written for a general audience. The newsletter isn't intended for children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time. You can also ask what information we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We'll reply as soon as we can, usually within a few days.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If anything here changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top. For significant changes, we'll also let newsletter subscribers know.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose { margin-top: 32px; }
</style>
